quiz 3 | What is a light-year?
* A distance
o A time
o A speed
o A brightness
= About 9.46 trillion km.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which was the first spacecraft to land humans on the Moon?
* Apollo 11
o Apollo 13
o Vostok 1
o Gemini 4
= 20 July 1969.
> Next

quiz 3 | The nearest star to the Sun is…
* Proxima Centauri
o Sirius
o Betelgeuse
o Polaris
= About 4.24 light-years away.
> Next

quiz 4 | Roughly how old is the universe?
* 13.8 billion years
o 4.5 billion years
o 100 billion years
o 6,000 years
= 4.5 billion is the age of the Earth and Sun.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which planet is known as the Red Planet?
* Mars
o Jupiter
o Venus
o Mercury
= Iron oxide (rust) dust colours its surface.
> Next

quiz 4 | What keeps the International Space Station in orbit?
* Its sideways speed while falling toward Earth
o Zero gravity at that height
o Rocket engines firing constantly
o The Moon's pull
= Gravity there is about 90% of surface gravity.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which telescope launched on Christmas Day 2021?
* James Webb Space Telescope
o Hubble
o Kepler
o Chandra
= It orbits the L2 point about 1.5 million km from Earth.
